WEBVTT

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:01.040
If you want to set up

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:03.219
operational monitoring, the logical

00:00:03.219 --> 00:00:05.000
conditions you can set are currently

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.820
quite primitive. The documentation

00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:08.820
notes that it struggles with combined

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:11.220
and conditions and it struggles with

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:13.680
aggregations. So I can't build a

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.760
monitor that says alert me of

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:17.820
the temperature drops and the store

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:20.500
is priority and the total aggregated

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:21.880
revenue is over $10 ,000.

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:24.560
In the current preview, stringing complex,

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:26.740
multi -variable logic like that into

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:29.000
a passive monitor is highly problematic

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:30.280
and likely to fail.

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:31.580
You have to keep the monitoring

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:33.519
conditions very simple and isolated.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:36.060
Furthermore, the operational agent

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:37.680
operates on a fixed five -minute

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:39.660
cycle. It is not sub -second

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:41.760
real time. It only checks the

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:42.839
condition every five minutes.
